 start in this business you  need to make the time you need to make  it a priority I need to stop making  excuses again you are where you are  right now because of you that's it that  might be a harsh truth but until you  recognize that you're never going to  grow as long as you blame the other  people as long as you're blaming  something else something else out there  besides the person that you can look at  in the mirror until you take that  responsibility until you accept that  role until you fully believe that I have  the power to change my circumstances and  I am the only one to blame do you really  believe that you're going to stay where  you look so stop making excuses  number three is stop criticizing  yourself  I think we're too hard on ourselves as  human beings but especially as  entrepreneurs we have these big bold  ideas and then immediately we start  thinking well Who am I to do that I  can't do that I didn't go to school for  that you know I'm not good enough to do  that I tried doing that once and it  didn't work out and we're constantly  beating ourselves down you look at how  entrepreneurs price their products and  services and it's often way lower than  it than what it should be  and until you start valuing your time  your experience the way it should then  other people won't value you either  right people will value you the way you  value yourself people will treat you the  way you treat yourself so if you're  constantly beating yourself down other  people will beat you down too and so you  need to start building up the confidence  in yourself you need to create a great  environment around yourself that helps  you believe in yourself more and believe  that you can play a game that's up here  instead of the one that's down here so  stop criticizing yourself you start  believing in yourself  number four is you need to stop settling  and this is a really tough one  because I think we settle way too much  you know we have these standards and  then we let them slide and we settle for  things that are that are just good you  know we put a lot of work into something  and then we see how much work it would  need to take to get it to that next step  and so we we don't do it we settle we  stop and too many people settle for  average you settle for mediocre you set  up we're just okay in all areas of your  life right you settle for an okay  relationship you set up for okay  customers you set up for an okay  business you never push yourself to go  for something great and if it's if it's  really bad you're going to change it  right if you have really bad customers  who are just yelling at you all the time  then you're going to fire them and move  on but it's the customers that are just  okay and a product that it's just okay  and the husband or wife that is just  okay or the relationship that's just  okay it's just good until you never  change it and you settle for good and if  you want to go and do something great  then you have to have high standards and  you have to stick to those standards  standards in in how other people treat  you and standards in how you treat  yourself stop settling for okay and  average and start achieving to higher  standards  number five you need to stop living  someone else's life  too often we make decisions in our life  in our business based on what other  people want right your parents want you  to do something your customers want you  to do something you know your friends  want you to do something Society wants  to do something and you're spending so  much of your time living up to other  people's expectations that you don't  ever even create a life of your own you  do this because it's what you're  expected to do not because what you want  to do and what you really want to do is  hard because that path isn't defined you  don't know how it's going to work out  you're drawn into a direction but you  don't know if that path is going to work  or not and it's scary and it's risky and  you don't have the people behind you to  go and make that happen and so because  it's so scary you don't do it where if  you live up to somebody else's  expectations that's defined right like  hey I want you to do this I want you to  take care of that and so it's easier to  do that because there is that path but  you're helping build somebody else's  dream instead of working on building  your own you need to stop living other  people's lives and start living your  version of your life  number six is stop complaining people  from my experience who are huge  complainers don't get very far when you  talk to burn you ask how their day is  going all you hear is negativity law  this didn't work out and all that guy is  such an idiot and you know just one  negative thing after another where it is  really hard being an entrepreneur right  it's going to be one of the hardest  thing to ever do in your life and the  thing that gets you through is one the  love for what you're doing and to the  optimism that it's going to work out  like you have to hold on to goodness to  get you through all the crap that's  involved in running a business and  successful entrepreneurs are never the  complainers they're never the ones who  are blaming other people back to the top  of the episode but they aren't the ones  who just walk in every day and are just  complaining about things and yes you  have really really bad down dates and  it's not that you're always optimistic  100% of the time but you do not want to  be the person who is just constantly  complaining and to take it a bit further  you don't want to be surrounded by  people who are constantly complaining  because they bring you down and their  negative energy makes you be more of a  complainer where if you surround  yourself with people who are uplifting  optimistic who believe who are trying to  do big things  then you will as well and you will  eventually do those big projects and  achieve your goals  so stop complaining and start being more  optimistic  and number seven is stop talking and  start doing how many people do you know  who just talk a big game you talk about  the things that one day they're going to  do that someday is on their plan that  just keep adding to their bucket list  and never actually do it the people who  just have all these great ideas but then  they sit at a job working on the 5 that  they hate and they never follow through  on any of the things that they have  these big dreams for stop being a talker  stop being the person who just shouts  out ideas and then gets upset when  somebody else goes and does it that's  not their fault for beating you to your  idea you didn't execute that's on you if  you have something that you want to do  go out and start doing it it may be some  big dream and that's amazing but find  the smallest way to get started you want  to dream big and start small a lot of  people have these big dreams and they  don't know where to start there's no  magical one beautiful place to start you  just start you start and you take  another step and you take another step  and as you start taking your steps the  path reveals itself where so many people  are too afraid to take that first step  they don't know how to get started and  then that dream just stays there is a  dream and then you watch somebody else  go and execute and achieve that dream  instead of you so stop talking stop  talking about the things that one day  you're going to do and start doing so  those are the seven things that I think  you need to stop doing right now if you  want to start achieving success in your  business I'd love to know what you think  of the 7 I'd love to know which of the  ones is holding you back the most right  now be honest leave in the comments  below and if you think I'm missing  something from the list add it in as  well in the comments and I will join the  discussion thank you guys so much for  watching  continue to believe and I'll see you  soon

